# Per-workspace app state (window layout, restored tabs, saved pane trees).
# Listed explicitly: it was only being ignored as a side effect of the `*.tedi`
# theme-file pattern further down, so renaming that pattern would have started
# committing local session state.
.tedi/
.local/

# Recovered WinSCP credentials — local only, never commit
plan.txt
check-public-ip.ps1

# react-doctor: local-only scan config (rule policy kept off the repo)
react-doctor.config.json

# Project-local working files
/icon.png
# Both cases on purpose. Ignore patterns are matched case-SENSITIVELY, so the
# uppercase spelling alone only worked here because Windows sets
# core.ignorecase=true; a Linux clone would have offered `todo.md` for commit.
TODO.MD
todo.md
REMOTE-ACCESS-SPEC.md
FEATURE-STUDY.md
# Exported theme files are personal / test artifacts, not repo content.
*.tedi

# Extensions are developed in this workspace but pushed to their own
# repos (each one has its own .git, README, LICENSE, release CI). Keep
# the working copies on disk for local iteration but never commit them
# to the TEDI main repo.
/extensions/*/
!/extensions/README.md
# Local linker override (rust-lld instead of MSVC link.exe). It belongs to a
# machine, not to the repo: committing it would also decide the linker for CI
# and for the signed release installers, and CI only ever builds in debug, so a
# release built that way would reach users untested. Keep it local until one
# release build has been through it deliberately.
/src-tauri/.cargo/

# The project-level MCP registration, written by the plug button in the header
# (or by `claude mcp add`). It names an ABSOLUTE path to the server bundled in
# THIS machine's TEDI install, so it is a per-developer file by construction:
# committing one hands everyone else a path that does not exist on their disk.
# It used to be tracked with a relative `scripts/mcp/server.mjs`, which worked
# only from a repo checkout and, being invisible to the header switch, meant an
# agent kept loading TEDI's MCP after that switch was turned off.
/.mcp.json
